{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Thus says your brother Israel… You know all the hardship…</b> For this hardship was rightfully half yours to bear in paying off the debt of 'for your seed shall be a stranger' (Genesis 15:13), yet we bore all the hardship in its entirety — even your portion. And he hinted in the word 'הַתְּלָאָה,' which adds up to ת״ (400), corresponding to the four hundred years of exile, plus forty more that they were tossed about in the wilderness, and the א׳ (1) is not counted in the reckoning. And just as you have no share in the payment of the debt, so you have no share in the land — for it is as though we acquired your portion from your hand, and it is fitting that you too should place the purchase in our hands and assist us to come to the land swiftly."], :book :numbers, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:42:10.838888279Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}